{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/993083-keepers-of-the-word-vs-pancryptiates-oh-my","id":993083,"title":"Keepers of the Word VS Pancryptiates, oh my","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-25T13:53:00-07:00","id":993083,"title":"Keepers of the Word VS Pancryptiates, oh my","content":"Hi!<br /> <br /> I can swear to you, I read and read and cannot for the life of me make out what are the fundamental differences between both Orders, the big daddy and mommy of their own prodigal son, the Mysterium. I've compiled a list of statements, taken mostly from the Mysterium order book, the 2nd Edition core book and the Dark Eras chapter, &quot;To the Strongest&quot;. Could you please confirm whether any of these statements are true, false or capriciously misleading?<br /> <br /> <u><b>Keepers of the Word:</b></u><ul><li>Initially composed of Greek and Egyptian sorcerers from the Jnanashakti school of magic (or Darshana).</li> <li>Their agenda is pretty straightforward: uncover magical secrets, learn magic and teach those secrets to those who are deemed worthy.</li> <li>They created the first Athenea.</li> <li>Accused of aggresively pursuing mysteries, often at the expense of the other orders (that means theft, at the very least).</li> <li>Had an allegedly overcomplicated system of advancement through the cult, comprised of an infinite number of levels of initiation, each level granting greater magical secrets. In reality, most mages never reached the superior levels, and thus the knowledge of upper echelons could get lost.</li> </ul><br /> <u><b>Pancryptiates:</b></u><ul><li>Initially composed of Persian and Indian sorcerers from the Jnanashakti school of magic (Darshana).</li> <li>Their agenda revolved around the theory that, after the Fall, magic gets diluted and corrupted the more it stays in the Falllen World. Therefore, they were more concerned with acquiring knowledge in order to preserve it from further obscuration, concentrating in cataloguing, archiving and studying said secrets.</li> <li>They created the Egregore. They also created the role of Savant: a mage commiting all sorts of knowledge to memory and hermitaging in order to better preserve it.</li> <li>One of the first groups in studying the Abyss, the Curse of Quiescence and and the gradual loss of magic from the Fallen World.</li> <li>At first following and advancement system similar to the Keepers, they reformed its initiation levels and reduced them to five. Gained more popularity and recruits as a result from this reform.</li> </ul><br /> Well, what do you think? Would you add something else, delete it, or denounce it as pure myth or worst?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","name":"Zooroos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T14:12:57-07:00","id":993094,"title":"","content":"You take it wrong. Probably cause best Orders creation is understand as <b>process</b>. But maybe my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/387074-history-of-awakened-mage-timeline\">fanon timeline compilation</a> based on gameline books will show you more on both groups origins and by this, their profile...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/387074-history-of-awakened-mage-timeline#post387074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>334 BCE:</b> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aristotle\" target=\"_blank\">Aristotle</a> founds <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peripatetic_school\" target=\"_blank\">Peripatetic school</a> in the Lyceum of Athens. Some of his students are Awakened. Sorcerers under it are starting to using term \u2018Atlantis\u2019 for probable ideal society from Time Before they want to reflect. ( <b><i>To The Strongest</i> - Dark Eras</b> )<br /> <br /> <b>323 BCE: </b>Aristotle must run with his family from Athens, because his critique of government. His Awakened followers from Gnostikon Darshana cult call it <b><i>Keepers of the Word</i></b>, as they sworn to uncover as much of knowledge they can in their lifetime. Groups splints when their mentor is leaving them. With Eastern sorcerers travelling in Empire working on very similar principle, group starts to join, meet and spread on Mediterranean Sea area. ( <b>Fan</b>, based on <b>Mysterium</b> and <b><i>To The Strongest</i> - Dark Eras </b>)<br /> <br /> <b>297- 283</b> <b>BCE: </b>Demetrius of Phalerum, Athenian orator, student of <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Theophrastus\" target=\"_blank\">Theophrastus</a> and Aristotel, is banished from his homeland after ten years of governing Athens and living Thebes behind him, comes to the court of Alexandria. Under the rule of <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ptolemy_I_Soter\" target=\"_blank\">Ptolemy I Soter</a> he creates Library of Alexandria. Even if he probably were not the sorcerer, his students and colleges were - and they all created Gnostikon Darshana cult of preserving all knowledge. Even after the exile of Demetrius by the Ptolemy II, cult inside the Library thrive. This group would call itself <b><i>Pancryptiates</i></b> and created first in known Atheneum in Great Library of Alexandria. In years to come, Pancrypties would spread on all former Alexandrian Empire, by the trade of books it copied and preserved. ( <b>Fan</b>, based on <b>Mysterium</b> )<br /> <br /> <b>241 BCE:</b> On the final return to the Italy, first European Caucus of Adamantine Arrow has gathered, from the veterans of this long lasting war. In the shadows of Rome, Arrows sworn to defend the Republic, both Sleepers and Awakened.<b> Keepers of the Word</b> and <b>Pancryptiates</b> already took first steps in the city.( <b>Fan</b> )<br /> <br /> <b>218-201 BCE:</b> Second Punic War. When Hannibal challenged Rome, almost all of Adamantine Arrow joined Legions in defend of Republic, before his army would crash the Italy. With enemies at their doorstep, occult conflicts were paused. The more armies gone to South, the more inside the Sanate itself the other war was done - free of Arrows watchful eyes, young Silver Ladder were fighting with Guardians over the vision for the Republic. This secret conflict quickly changed idealized forefathers of Tearchs in to power hungry stereotype of Lions that need to much. But the occult war made Guardians into caucus itself, going for every help they could grasp for - using the tools of their brothers in other countries, they started first Roman Labyrinth to gain support. Both new Orders gathered people, influence and backing by proxy of their cults inside Rome\u2019s elite. <b>Keepers of the Word</b> and <b>Pancryptiates</b> do not take active role in this occult conflict, they were strengthening their positions in Rome. ( <b>Fan</b> )<br /> <br /> <b>145 BCE:</b> Ptolemy VIII expelled all foreign scholars from Alexandria, leading to diaspora of <i>Pancrypties </i>cult on the Mediterranean Sea area, and becoming of it the proper Order. ( <b>Fan</b> )<br /> <br /> <b>48 BCE: </b>Caesar burning and saking Alexandria. Great Library is largely damaged. Many of precious Artifacts in it\u2019s Atheneum is stolen. Pancryptiates are accusing Arrows of this \u201cbarbarianism\u201d, even if they know that Caesar was not Order\u2019s member. ( <b>Fan</b> )<br /> <br /> <b>12th century AD:</b> Pancryptiates and Keepers of the World Orders merged into one Mysterium in Byzantine Empire under Corpus Author that made hers Ascension from this event. Fall of Empire and Silk Road to Asia propagated unified Order. ( <b>Mysterium </b>)</div> </div> </div> </div>In nutshell, Order is superCult, on worldwide scale. <i>Keepers of Word</i> were dedicated to travel and uncovering knowledge. <i>Pancrypties </i>wanted to stop <i>Pancryptia </i>by sustaining long term lore, creating Athenea. First group are ancient Lara Croft and Indiana Jones, second ones are Hogwarts Hufflepuff House. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Corpus Author have proven them that they are both about uncovering lore, in long term, creating Mysterium as we know it in Byzantine Empire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-25-2016, 05:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T14:38:56-07:00","id":993106,"title":"","content":"I appreciate your candor, Wyrd, but that doesn't answer my question. What, if any, are the statements you find wrong and/or problematic about my initial post?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","name":"Zooroos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T15:36:53-07:00","id":993133,"title":"","content":"Basically the big difference is that the Keepers of the Word were more interested in preserving old magical stuff right where it was. The Pancryptiates were more aggressive and geographically active collectors of magical lore and artifacts hoping to beat Sleepers to sources of magic before Sleepers could wipe it out. Presumably there were greater differences between them at one point, but the work of the Corpus Author sufficiently blurred that line that they joined forces because she had in some ways rendered them practically identical. For instance the initiation levels they both exhibited were likely reformed by her to something that made some damn sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T21:54:57-07:00","id":993315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zooroos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/993083-keepers-of-the-word-vs-pancryptiates-oh-my?p=993106#post993106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I appreciate your candor, Wyrd, but that doesn't answer my question. What, if any, are the statements you find wrong and/or problematic about my initial post?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, let's break it then...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zooroos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/993083-keepers-of-the-word-vs-pancryptiates-oh-my#post993083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u><b>Keepers of the Word:</b></u>[*]Initially composed of Greek and Egyptian sorcerers from the Jnanashakti school of magic (or Darshana).</div> </div> </div> </div>Not true, original Keepers were following Aristoteles. They joined with similar groups from other Great Cults - mostly India - but very first group started in Greece.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zooroos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/993083-keepers-of-the-word-vs-pancryptiates-oh-my#post993083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]Their agenda is pretty straightforward: uncover magical secrets, learn magic and teach those secrets to those who are deemed worthy.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is accurate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zooroos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/993083-keepers-of-the-word-vs-pancryptiates-oh-my#post993083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]They created the first Athenea.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, Pancryptiates created Athenea system to sustain lore.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zooroos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/993083-keepers-of-the-word-vs-pancryptiates-oh-my#post993083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]Accused of aggresively pursuing mysteries, often at the expense of the other orders (that means theft, at the very least)..</div> </div> </div> </div>Accurate, Keepers of Word are Ravenclaw House of Hogwarts. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zooroos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/993083-keepers-of-the-word-vs-pancryptiates-oh-my#post993083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]Had an allegedly overcomplicated system of advancement through the cult, comprised of an infinite number of levels of initiation, each level granting greater magical secrets. In reality, most mages never reached the superior levels, and thus the knowledge of upper echelons could get lost.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is accurate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zooroos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/993083-keepers-of-the-word-vs-pancryptiates-oh-my#post993083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u><b>Pancryptiates:</b></u>[*]Initially composed of Persian and Indian sorcerers from the Jnanashakti school of magic (Darshana).</div> </div> </div> </div>Pointed before - as started in Alexandria, they were on first Hellenistic Egyptians. Quickly they spread on whole Mediteranina Sea are, so better is to talk about Hellenistic nations in general.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zooroos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/993083-keepers-of-the-word-vs-pancryptiates-oh-my#post993083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]Their agenda revolved around the theory that, after the Fall, magic gets diluted and corrupted the more it stays in the Falllen World. Therefore, they were more concerned with acquiring knowledge in order to preserve it from further obscuration, concentrating in cataloguing, archiving and studying said secrets.</div> </div> </div> </div>Accurate. It's also reason why they invented Athenea system.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zooroos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/993083-keepers-of-the-word-vs-pancryptiates-oh-my#post993083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]They created the Egregore. They also created the role of Savant: a mage commiting all sorts of knowledge to memory and hermitaging in order to better preserve it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Accurate. They seems on group that would work like this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zooroos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/993083-keepers-of-the-word-vs-pancryptiates-oh-my#post993083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]One of the first groups in studying the Abyss, the Curse of Quiescence and and the gradual loss of magic from the Fallen World.</div> </div> </div> </div>Acurate, they call it phenomena <i>Panscriptia</i> and it's even become name of their Order. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zooroos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/993083-keepers-of-the-word-vs-pancryptiates-oh-my#post993083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]At first following and advancement system similar to the Keepers, they reformed its initiation levels and reduced them to five. Gained more popularity and recruits as a result from this reform.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also accurate. Simplicity of Pancryptiates lead to them mostly overwhelming of Keepers. Middle Ages, with monastic culture also was great time for Pancryptiates.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-26-2016, 12:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T01:48:02-07:00","id":993383,"title":"","content":"While pointing out inaccuracies are fine, you still haven't said what make Pancryptiates different from Keepers of the Word <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1437_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1437\" data-vbnamecard=\"1437\">wyrdhamster</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T02:44:16-07:00","id":993401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/993083-keepers-of-the-word-vs-pancryptiates-oh-my?p=993315#post993315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not true, original Keepers were following Aristoteles. They joined with similar groups from other Great Cults - mostly India - but very first group started in Greece.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where does it say the orginal Keepers were followers of Aristotle?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No, Pancryptiates created Athenea system to sustain lore. </div> </div> </div>That was true in Mysterium (I think), but not anymore. 2e pg. 44 says the Keepers founded the first Athenaea.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is accurate. </div> </div> </div>I'd say it was accurate. Without Atlantis, the Keepers having a vast circle of degrees doesn't really make sense. I mean, the basic idea of circles of initiation is apparently an invention of the Arcadian cult. The Karpani and Mantrikis aren't organised that way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Pointed before - as started in Alexandria, they were on first Hellenistic Egyptians. Quickly they spread on whole Mediteranina Sea are, so better is to talk about Hellenistic nations in general. </div> </div> </div>Where are you getting that from? I can't find that anywhere. Also, I think you're confusing the origins of the two factions. In the Future Fates section, it describes the two factions without explicitly naming them, but it's pretty obvious which is which:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> One faction dominated by Pelasgians and Weret-Hekau seeks out magical Artifacts, texts, and wondrous places for their pragmatic virtues. They believe magi should use what they find to defeat ignorance and malefic sorcery. </div> </div> </div>That's clearly the Keepers.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> TheKarpani-dominated second group believes it incautious to harness these discoveries immediately, and concentrates on archiving, guarding, and carefully studying them. Mantriki prefer this approach, </div> </div> </div>That's the Pancryptiate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also accurate. Simplicity of Pancryptiates lead to them mostly overwhelming of Keepers. Middle Ages, with monastic culture also was great time for Pancryptiates. </div> </div> </div>Except that it's been heavily retconned since. The Mysterium book presented the conflict as being back in the mists of time after the Fall, but 2e moved it to the first millenium CE.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> While pointing out inaccuracies are fine, you still haven't said what make Pancryptiates different from Keepers of the Word </div> </div> </div>Wyrd already did that, but Zooroos specfically asked for inaccuracies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T03:45:02-07:00","id":993411,"title":"","content":"Thank you very much, everyone! I think now I'm confident about the actual differences between Keepers and Pancryptiates. My main point of dissonance before (no pun intended) is about the origin of Athenea. The 2E core book clearly states that were the Keepers the ones who founded the first Athenea, yet in the Mysterium book seemed to imply that the Pacryptiates created them. Which might be merely a trivial matter, since its clear that both Orders benefited and made extensive use of an Athenea-like system. However, it's quite telling to me that the first Athenea, following the Ethos of the Keepers, were probably a place for learning and divulgation and not solely as an archive, which would have probably been the case if Pancryptiates were the first to create them (or at least a Pancryptiates-only academy).<br /> <br /> The ethnic/cultural composition of the early orders was also a point of contention in my mind, perhaps because my headcanon was already taking into account Wyrd's Mage Timeline --which is excellent, I mean, but not exactly kosher either-- but &quot;To the Strongest&quot; Dark Era is pretty specific about it, as Michael has already pointed out.<br /> <br /> Mrmdubois did pose a pretty interesting hypothesis: that the Corpus Author &quot;blurred&quot; the lines that separated both Orders by incorporating them in her Omens. Taking into account how hard a time I'm having sifting through books and separating the two, I believe him. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The final point of frustration, one which I hadn't realized before, was the precise date ot the merging. Since it's not clear how did the Corpus Author retconned reality to acomodate for a seamless merging of both Orders, I think it's safe to assume the current, edited timeline is the most historically accurate (linearly accurate?). The 2E core book clearly states both Orders merged after the publication of the Corpus Mysteriorum, sometime during the 13th century, which is, what, high Middle Ages? But clearly in the 2nd millenium AD.<br /> <br /> Mmm, am I missing something?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","name":"Zooroos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T04:09:28-07:00","id":993417,"title":"","content":"We will mention the two Orders in the history chapter of Tome of the Pentacle (because hey - for the majority of its history the Diamond *did* have five members), but I'm pinning my hopes on Dark Eras 2 to finally give them separate splat pages.<br /> <br /> Remember what the Corpus Mysterium is about<b></b>: Neither Order had the tone statement the Mysterium does of &quot;magic is alive&quot;, because that was her Noumenon.<br /> <br /> The Keepers believed that they safeguarded *knowledge*, and had both proto-Athenea that didn't have the religious traits modern Athenea have, and a Guanxi-like economy of information. They thought that they were the last bastions of civilisation in a chaotic universe, and their internal disagreements were about whether it was better to influence Sleeper affairs by sharing technology and culture the Sleepers had lost versus preserving it for future need. They were like a cross between the Mysterium, Free Council, and Silver Ladder, with almost Seer-like leanings. Their tone statement could be &quot;magic has worth&quot; - both a price to be paid and value if taken from others.<br /> <br /> The Pancryptiates were smaller, weirder, and much more gnostic. They believed Sleepers actively damaged the world by existing, and sought to either remove themselves from the world and society or build bulwarks where the Abyss had less sway. The Keepers regarded all knowledge as at least partially magical - the Pancryptiates would be outraged by a Keeper storehouse keeping roman crop management manuals alongside the grimoires. They built demesnes, summoned supernal entities, studied the Abyss, explored Emanations and sought a way *out* of the Fallen World. They were like a cross between the Mysterium, Guardians, Arrow (they relished self-sacrifice for the cause, like becoming savants or jettisonning all mortal ties) and, in some ways, Tremere - they were deeply interested in the soul, and thought the world was evil.<br /> <br /> In a medieval setting, the Keepers would be monasteries and the Pancryptiates hermitage-dwelling poor friars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T05:03:47-07:00","id":993434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> yet in the Mysterium book seemed to imply that the Pacryptiates created them </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I suspect the answer is that Mysterium was written with the idea of a literal historical Atlantis in mind. It makes sense for the Pancryptiate to focus on preserving magical knowlege because they already have a large store of it from Atlantis. When 2e rewrote/recontextualised the history, that's no longer true.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zooroos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/993083-keepers-of-the-word-vs-pancryptiates-oh-my?p=993411#post993411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But clearly in the 2nd millenium AD.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it's my use of 1st millenium CE that's causing confusion, I was speaking loosly for brevity. Like, the era of two Orders is 2-3 hundred years either side of the first millenium. Sorry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T07:00:28-07:00","id":993477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/993083-keepers-of-the-word-vs-pancryptiates-oh-my?p=993417#post993417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We will mention the two Orders in the history chapter of Tome of the Pentacle (because hey - for the majority of its history the Diamond *did* have five members), but I'm pinning my hopes on Dark Eras 2 to finally give them separate splat pages.</div> </div> </div> </div> I hope it too, the line certainly deserves it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/993083-keepers-of-the-word-vs-pancryptiates-oh-my?p=993417#post993417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember what the Corpus Mysterium is about<b></b>: Neither Order had the tone statement the Mysterium does of &amp;quot;magic is alive&amp;quot;, because that was her Noumenon.</div> </div> </div> </div> Doh, of course you are right. Thanks for pointing that out!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/993083-keepers-of-the-word-vs-pancryptiates-oh-my?p=993417#post993417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Keepers believed that they safeguarded *knowledge*, and had both proto-Athenea that didn't have the religious traits modern Athenea have, and a Guanxi-like economy of information. They thought that they were the last bastions of civilisation in a chaotic universe, and their internal disagreements were about whether it was better to influence Sleeper affairs by sharing technology and culture the Sleepers had lost versus preserving it for future need. They were like a cross between the Mysterium, Free Council, and Silver Ladder, with almost Seer-like leanings. Their tone statement could be &amp;quot;magic has worth&amp;quot; - both a price to be paid and value if taken from others.</div> </div> </div> </div> So they thought of themselves as shepherds of civilization, mmm, much more social-oriented than I first thought...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/993083-keepers-of-the-word-vs-pancryptiates-oh-my?p=993417#post993417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Pancryptiates were smaller, weirder, and much more gnostic. They believed Sleepers actively damaged the world by existing, and sought to either remove themselves from the world and society or build bulwarks where the Abyss had less sway. The Keepers regarded all knowledge as at least partially magical - the Pancryptiates would be outraged by a Keeper storehouse keeping roman crop management manuals alongside the grimoires. They built demesnes, summoned supernal entities, studied the Abyss, explored Emanations and sought a way *out* of the Fallen World. They were like a cross between the Mysterium, Guardians, Arrow (they relished self-sacrifice for the cause, like becoming savants or jettisonning all mortal ties) and, in some ways, Tremere - they were deeply interested in the soul, and thought the world was evil.</div> </div> </div> </div> THAT I wanna play, like, right now <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">In a medieval setting, the Keepers would be monasteries and the Pancryptiates hermitage-dwelling poor friars.</div> </div> </div> </div> Pancryptiates definitely gave me a vibe of House Criamon from Ars Magica, and now it's even better explained and defined.<br /> <br /> Thanks Dave for lifting the curtain for us a little. Looking forward for all the Mage goodness coming our way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","name":"Zooroos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T07:06:01-07:00","id":993480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/993083-keepers-of-the-word-vs-pancryptiates-oh-my?p=993417#post993417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In a medieval setting, the Keepers would be monasteries and the Pancryptiates hermitage-dwelling poor friars.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks <b>Dave</b> for claryfication! Even I need now to rewrite fanon origins of those too...<br /> <br /> Maybe it's too simplistic, but does not this mean that Keepers of Word are basically lorekeepers ( and lore traders ) and Pancryptiates are extreme gnostics?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-26-2016, 10:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T11:37:49-07:00","id":993609,"title":"","content":"Pancryptiates are as gnostic as it gets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T21:45:09-08:00","id":1005592,"title":"","content":"So modern Mysterium's main thing is &quot;Magic is alive.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Keepers had &quot;Magic is power.&quot;<br /> <br /> What would the Pancryptiates have said, prolly?<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T21:47:34-08:00","id":1005593,"title":"","content":"Pancryptiates would have something like 'Magic is escape' - they want to check boundaries, best to leave this world all together.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T08:09:08-08:00","id":1006197,"title":"","content":"I'd argue that they don't want to leave the world behind, they want to escape Pancryptia so they can experience a pure, undiluted life of magic and mysteries. Personally, I'm inclined for a different motto: <b>&quot;Magic is Fading.&quot;</b> I like to think of the later Corpus Mysteriorum as a defiant counter-argument to that pessimistic world view: <b>Magic is Alive&quot;</b>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","name":"Zooroos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}